{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-95216","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-159104","text":"Board semantics — what the circuitry can and cannot carry, and the minimal obligation for more (proposal)"}]},{"id":"blk-95217","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159105","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: PROPOSAL. Nothing here changes WRL Core 0.1.2 (frozen), the forge, or any identity."},{"id":"spn-159106","text":" Written 2026-09-13 for the WRL lane, beside "},{"id":"spn-159107","marks":["code"],"text":"BOOK_SURFACE_PROFILE_PROPOSAL.md"},{"id":"spn-159108","text":" and the pending "},{"id":"spn-159109","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.semantic.v3"},{"id":"spn-159110","text":" obligation. Measured at WRL "},{"id":"spn-159111","marks":["code"],"text":"32160fec77a1"},{"id":"spn-159112","text":", TRVM "},{"id":"spn-159113","marks":["code"],"text":"bf8670d57347"},{"id":"spn-159114","text":", over the book's circuit board ("},{"id":"spn-159115","marks":["code"],"text":"_patterns/wrl/chain/"},{"id":"spn-159116","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159117","marks":["code"],"text":"_conclusion.wrl"},{"id":"spn-159118","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-95218","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159119","marks":["bold"],"text":"The question (Travis, 2026-09-13):"},{"id":"spn-159120","text":" "},{"id":"spn-159121","marks":["italic"],"text":"does this circuitry handle input and output parameters, variables, settings or configuration?"},{"id":"spn-159122","text":" This document answers from the language's own tables, states what the book had to do by convention, and proposes the smallest additions that would make those conventions language."}]},{"id":"blk-95219","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-159123","text":"0. What the board is, and what the book had to fake"}]},{"id":"blk-95220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159124","text":"The board is one WRL world: 111 objects, 101 wires, 9 clock domains, 40 relays, 17 doors, 22 inter-chapter links; sealed at every chapter ("},{"id":"spn-159125","marks":["code"],"text":"P17"},{"id":"spn-159126","text":" refuses a step that drops anything); reduced whole by the forge. To make 32 chapters compose into it, the book used four conventions "},{"id":"spn-159127","marks":["bold"],"text":"that are not in the language"},{"id":"spn-159128","text":":"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-95222","spans":[{"id":"spn-159129","text":"Convention"}]},{"id":"blk-95223","spans":[{"id":"spn-159130","text":"Count"}]},{"id":"blk-95224","spans":[{"id":"spn-159131","text":"What it stands in for"}]}],"id":"blk-95221","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-95225","spans":[{"id":"spn-159132","text":"an id prefix per chapter ("},{"id":"spn-159133","marks":["code"],"text":"lc_"},{"id":"spn-159134","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159135","marks":["code"],"text":"rj_"},{"id":"spn-159136","text":", …)"}]},{"id":"blk-95226","spans":[{"id":"spn-159137","text":"32"}]},{"id":"blk-95227","spans":[{"id":"spn-159138","text":"a "},{"id":"spn-159139","marks":["bold"],"text":"module boundary"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95228","spans":[{"id":"spn-159140","text":"an entry relay with an open input port ("},{"id":"spn-159141","marks":["code"],"text":"<pfx>_in"},{"id":"spn-159142","text":", or a router such as "},{"id":"spn-159143","marks":["code"],"text":"lc_thread"},{"id":"spn-159144","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159145","marks":["code"],"text":"rj_r"},{"id":"spn-159146","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159147","marks":["code"],"text":"cc_grant"},{"id":"spn-159148","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-95229","spans":[{"id":"spn-159149","text":"21"}]},{"id":"blk-95230","spans":[{"id":"spn-159150","text":"a module's "},{"id":"spn-159151","marks":["bold"],"text":"input port"},{"id":"spn-159152","text":" — one per bench"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95231","spans":[{"id":"spn-159153","text":"a test bench ("},{"id":"spn-159154","marks":["code"],"text":"<id>.bench.wrl"},{"id":"spn-159155","text":": a pulser driving the entry), used for the module's own film only"}]},{"id":"blk-95232","spans":[{"id":"spn-159156","text":"21"}]},{"id":"blk-95233","spans":[{"id":"spn-159157","text":"a "},{"id":"spn-159158","marks":["bold"],"text":"harness"},{"id":"spn-159159","text":"; never part of the chain"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95234","spans":[{"id":"spn-159160","text":"links ("},{"id":"spn-159161","marks":["code"],"text":"<id>.links.wrl"},{"id":"spn-159162","text":": an earlier router's output into this entry), used only in the chain"}]},{"id":"blk-95235","spans":[{"id":"spn-159163","text":"22"}]},{"id":"blk-95236","spans":[{"id":"spn-159164","marks":["bold"],"text":"instantiation / wiring"},{"id":"spn-159165","text":" of a module"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95237","spans":[{"id":"spn-159166","text":"a "},{"id":"spn-159167","marks":["code"],"text":"ScenarioV1"},{"id":"spn-159168","text":" per module (23), the forge's own run-input document, bound to the module's id"}]},{"id":"blk-95238","spans":[{"id":"spn-159169","text":"23"}]},{"id":"blk-95239","spans":[{"id":"spn-159170","marks":["bold"],"text":"runtime inputs"},{"id":"spn-159171","text":" — the one convention that is already language"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-95240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159172","marks":["code"],"text":"chain.mjs"},{"id":"spn-159173","text":" composes these textually; wrl.js seals the result. Every one of these conventions is honest, and every one is invisible to WRL: a fragment is just declarations and edges."}]},{"id":"blk-95241","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-159174","text":"1. What WRL Core has (from "},{"id":"spn-159175","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl.js"},{"id":"spn-159176","text":"'s frozen tables)"}]},{"id":"blk-95242","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159177","marks":["bold"],"text":"Static configuration, part of identity."},{"id":"spn-159178","text":" "},{"id":"spn-159179","marks":["code"],"text":"Pulser"},{"id":"spn-159180","text":": "},{"id":"spn-159181","marks":["code"],"text":"mode"},{"id":"spn-159182","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159183","marks":["code"],"text":"period"},{"id":"spn-159184","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159185","marks":["code"],"text":"phase"},{"id":"spn-159186","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159187","marks":["code"],"text":"epoch"},{"id":"spn-159188","text":" (sugar "},{"id":"spn-159189","marks":["code"],"text":"every K, phase P"}]}],"id":"blk-95243","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-95245","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159190","text":"/ "},{"id":"spn-159191","marks":["code"],"text":"once at E"},{"id":"spn-159192","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-159193","marks":["code"],"text":"Spinner"},{"id":"spn-159194","text":": "},{"id":"spn-159195","marks":["code"],"text":"w"},{"id":"spn-159196","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159197","marks":["code"],"text":"n"},{"id":"spn-159198","text":", a four-lane "},{"id":"spn-159199","marks":["code"],"text":"rotor"},{"id":"spn-159200","text":" (or a named one: "},{"id":"spn-159201","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-159202","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159203","marks":["code"],"text":"reverse_x/y/z"},{"id":"spn-159204","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159205","marks":["code"],"text":"quarter_turn_z"},{"id":"spn-159206","text":" by sugar) and "},{"id":"spn-159207","marks":["code"],"text":"configurable"},{"id":"spn-159208","text":". "},{"id":"spn-159209","marks":["code"],"text":"Mailbox"},{"id":"spn-159210","text":": "},{"id":"spn-159211","marks":["code"],"text":"w"},{"id":"spn-159212","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159213","marks":["code"],"text":"cap"},{"id":"spn-159214","text":" — unwritable in source. "},{"id":"spn-159215","marks":["code"],"text":"Relay"},{"id":"spn-159216","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159217","marks":["code"],"text":"Door"},{"id":"spn-159218","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159219","marks":["code"],"text":"Orb"},{"id":"spn-159220","text":": none. Any change moves the "},{"id":"spn-159221","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-"},{"id":"spn-159222","text":" id."}]},{"id":"blk-95246","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159223","marks":["bold"],"text":"I/O is fixed port signatures."},{"id":"spn-159224","text":" "},{"id":"spn-159225","marks":["code"],"text":"Pulser{sig_out}"},{"id":"spn-159226","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159227","marks":["code"],"text":"Relay{sig_in, sig_out}"},{"id":"spn-159228","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159229","marks":["code"],"text":"Door{sig_in}"},{"id":"spn-159230","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-95247","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-95249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159231","marks":["code"],"text":"Spinner{sig_in, socket}"},{"id":"spn-159232","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159233","marks":["code"],"text":"Orb{pose}"},{"id":"spn-159234","text":". The "},{"id":"spn-159235","marks":["code"],"text":"{…}"},{"id":"spn-159236","text":" group is a checked projection, not a definition."}]},{"id":"blk-95250","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159237","marks":["bold"],"text":"Two wire types, one of them valued."},{"id":"spn-159238","text":" "},{"id":"spn-159239","marks":["code"],"text":"SignalWire"},{"id":"spn-159240","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-159241","marks":["code"],"text":"--sig-->"},{"id":"spn-159242","text":") carries one bit per epoch ("},{"id":"spn-159243","marks":["code"],"text":"cur=0|1"},{"id":"spn-159244","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-95251","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-95253","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159245","marks":["code"],"text":"SocketControl"},{"id":"spn-159246","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-159247","marks":["code"],"text":"--socket-->"},{"id":"spn-159248","text":") carries the spinner's "},{"id":"spn-159249","marks":["bold"],"text":"four rotor lanes"},{"id":"spn-159250","text":" into the orb's pose — so WRL already has a typed, valued wire; it has exactly one, and it is fixed to Spinner→Orb."}]},{"id":"blk-95254","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159251","marks":["bold"],"text":"At most one edge on any input port; fan-out unrestricted."},{"id":"spn-159252","text":" This is what makes relays routers and doors"}]}],"id":"blk-95255","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-95257","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159253","text":"latching switches, and what made two producers into one Door the language's own refusing join."}]},{"id":"blk-95258","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159254","marks":["bold"],"text":"Runtime state lives in the Film"},{"id":"spn-159255","text":", not in source: rotor and pose lanes, "},{"id":"spn-159256","marks":["code"],"text":"open"},{"id":"spn-159257","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159258","marks":["code"],"text":"cur_out"},{"id":"spn-159259","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159260","marks":["code"],"text":"armed/done/nf"},{"id":"spn-159261","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-95259","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-95261","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159262","text":"the orb's numeric-fault latch, and the claim/receipt/recognition projection."}]},{"id":"blk-95262","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95264","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159263","marks":["bold"],"text":"Runtime inputs are a separate document by design (D3)."},{"id":"spn-159264","text":" A claim in world source is refused"}]}],"id":"blk-95263","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-95265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159265","text":"("},{"id":"spn-159266","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_WORLD_SOURCE_HAS_SCENARIO"},{"id":"spn-159267","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-159268","marks":["code"],"text":"ScenarioV1"},{"id":"spn-159269","text":" carries "},{"id":"spn-159270","marks":["code"],"text":"initial_runtime.numeric_faults"},{"id":"spn-159271","text":" and one claim batch per epoch — "},{"id":"spn-159272","marks":["code"],"text":"SetRotor(spinner, r0.r1.r2.r3)"},{"id":"spn-159273","text":" (accepted only if the spinner is "},{"id":"spn-159274","marks":["code"],"text":"configurable"},{"id":"spn-159275","text":") and "},{"id":"spn-159276","marks":["code"],"text":"ResetFault(orb)"},{"id":"spn-159277","text":" — with writer ids and sequences; it has its own identity, the "},{"id":"spn-159278","marks":["bold"],"text":"ScenarioDigest"},{"id":"spn-159279","text":", and a "},{"id":"spn-159280","marks":["code"],"text":"ReplayBundleID = H(SemanticArtifactID, ScenarioDigest, initial runtime)"},{"id":"spn-159281","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-95266","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159282","marks":["bold"],"text":"Bounded admission."},{"id":"spn-159283","text":" "},{"id":"spn-159284","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_BATCH = 4"},{"id":"spn-159285","text":" claims per epoch, "},{"id":"spn-159286","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS = MAX_EVENTS = 6"},{"id":"spn-159287","text":" per world: a world of"}]}],"id":"blk-95267","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-95269","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159288","text":"111 objects admits at most six facts in total before the capacity fault latches. The board therefore runs on its clocks alone; its modules carry their claims in their own films."}]},{"id":"blk-95270","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95272","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159289","marks":["bold"],"text":"Settings that do not change meaning:"},{"id":"spn-159290","text":" the lowering profile ("},{"id":"spn-159291","marks":["code"],"text":"counter_encoding"},{"id":"spn-159292","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159293","marks":["code"],"text":"onehot_max"},{"id":"spn-159294","text":", …) moves the"}]}],"id":"blk-95271","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-95273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159295","marks":["code"],"text":"BackendArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-159296","text":" and leaves the "},{"id":"spn-159297","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-159298","text":" fixed."}]},{"id":"blk-95274","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-159299","text":"2. What it does not have"}]},{"id":"blk-95275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159300","text":"No variables. No expressions or arithmetic. No parameters on declarations beyond the fixed config keys. No user-declared ports. No module, import or instantiation construct. No valued wire other than socket→pose. No way to carry a value from one spinner's lanes into another object's input. The board's \"routers\" route a bit; its \"switches\" latch on a bit."}]},{"id":"blk-95276","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-159301","text":"3. Measured: what the book did with what exists, and what each chapter had to say instead"}]},{"id":"blk-95277","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159302","text":"Ten chapters use claims (ScenarioV1) as their inputs; two use a seeded fault; one uses a determinism double-run; twenty-one use a bench; twenty-two are wired by links; two are the empty world. Where a chapter's idea needed a value to flow (Semantic Membrane's \"what crosses the boundary\", Projection's \"derived view\"), the book used the one valued wire, socket→pose, and said so; where it needed a parameter (Progress-Aware Placement's \"where progress is greatest\"), it used topology (which home is wired) and said the number is unrun."}]},{"id":"blk-95278","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-159303","text":"4. The minimal obligation, in three steps of increasing cost"}]},{"id":"blk-95279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159304","marks":["bold"],"text":"Step 0 — done, and needs no ruling: adopt `ScenarioV1`."},{"id":"spn-159305","text":" The book's ad-hoc sidecars were converted to the forge's document, validated by "},{"id":"spn-159306","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_scenario_v1"},{"id":"spn-159307","text":", bound to each module's "},{"id":"spn-159308","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-159309","text":" (a mismatch refuses: "},{"id":"spn-159310","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_SCENARIO_WORLD_MISMATCH"},{"id":"spn-159311","text":"), and digested; every module page prints the ScenarioDigest beside the world id. Runtime inputs now have the identity the forge gives them."}]},{"id":"blk-95280","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159312","marks":["bold"],"text":"Step 1 — a module boundary as data, not syntax (a V2 static profile row, no runtime)."},{"id":"spn-159313","text":" Exactly what §0's conventions state: a "},{"id":"spn-159314","marks":["code"],"text":"MODULE"},{"id":"spn-159315","text":" role with attributes "},{"id":"spn-159316","marks":["code"],"text":"{prefix, entry, exits}"},{"id":"spn-159317","text":"; kinds "},{"id":"spn-159318","marks":["code"],"text":"CONTAINS [MODULE, *]"},{"id":"spn-159319","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159320","marks":["code"],"text":"ENTERS [SignalWire-source, MODULE]"},{"id":"spn-159321","text":" (a link into an entry), "},{"id":"spn-159322","marks":["code"],"text":"BENCHES [MODULE, Pulser]"},{"id":"spn-159323","text":" (the harness, excluded from the chain's identity). This makes the board's structure sealable and checkable — \"chapter 12 draws from chapter 10's router\" becomes a relation with an id — and adds no execution. Same path as "},{"id":"spn-159324","marks":["code"],"text":"book.surface.v1"},{"id":"spn-159325","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-95281","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159326","marks":["bold"],"text":"Step 2 — instance parameters (Core, not V2; needs a ruling on identity)."},{"id":"spn-159327","text":" A declaration-level parameter is already what "},{"id":"spn-159328","marks":["code"],"text":"period"},{"id":"spn-159329","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159330","marks":["code"],"text":"phase"},{"id":"spn-159331","text":", "},{"id":"spn-159332","marks":["code"],"text":"rotor"},{"id":"spn-159333","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-159334","marks":["code"],"text":"configurable"},{"id":"spn-159335","text":" are. The obligation is to say whether a "},{"id":"spn-159336","marks":["italic"],"text":"module"},{"id":"spn-159337","text":" may carry named parameters that its members' config keys reference ("},{"id":"spn-159338","marks":["code"],"text":"(every $rate)"},{"id":"spn-159339","text":"), and whether they enter identity (the sealed value) or the run (a scenario field). The identity-bearing reading is the one the frozen tables already take for every config key; the run-bearing reading is what "},{"id":"spn-159340","marks":["code"],"text":"SetRotor"},{"id":"spn-159341","text":" already is for one key. Recommendation: parameters are identity; runtime overrides are claims; do not add a third kind."}]},{"id":"blk-95282","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159342","marks":["bold"],"text":"Step 3 — valued wires beyond socket→pose (a new edge kind; a runtime change in TRVM)."},{"id":"spn-159343","text":" Carrying lanes from a spinner into a relay or another spinner is a new "},{"id":"spn-159344","marks":["code"],"text":"EDGE_KIND"},{"id":"spn-159345","text":" with a new port pair and reducer rules, subject to Law 6 (the carried value must be in the Film) and to the cost cliff (the term grows with width). This is the only step that touches the forge's reduction; it is the one this document does "},{"id":"spn-159346","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-159347","text":" recommend starting before steps 1 and 2 are ruled."}]},{"id":"blk-95283","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-159348","text":"5. What the book does meanwhile"}]},{"id":"blk-95284","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159349","text":"Keeps the conventions, states them on every page (fragment, bench, links, ScenarioV1 with its digest), and keeps the checks that make them honest: the seal at every step, the superset refusal, the completeness check that every sink changes by the last epoch, reducer parity where the native binary can parse the term."}]},{"id":"blk-95285","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-159350","text":"6. Not done here"}]},{"id":"blk-95286","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159351","text":"No row added, no edge kind, no parameter syntax, no identity moved. Two facts recorded for the TRVM lane: the native reducer refuses the whole board and two small modules at parse (exit 4; "},{"id":"spn-159352","marks":["code"],"text":"MAXNAMES 8192"},{"id":"spn-159353","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-159354","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32.c"},{"id":"spn-159355","text":" suspected, unconfirmed), and "},{"id":"spn-159356","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS = 6"},{"id":"spn-159357","text":" bounds a world's claims regardless of its size."}]},{"id":"blk-95287","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-159358","text":"Questions for adjudication"}]},{"id":"blk-95288","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95290","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159359","text":"Is a module boundary a V2 static row (structure only) or a Core 0.2 construct (with a text surface)?"}]}],"id":"blk-95289","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95292","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159360","text":"Do module parameters enter identity, the run, or is the question refused because config keys already are"}]}],"id":"blk-95291","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-95293","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159361","text":"the parameters?"}]},{"id":"blk-95294","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95296","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159362","text":"Should a bench be representable at all in the language, or is \"harness ≠ world\" a rule worth keeping as"}]}],"id":"blk-95295","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-95297","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159363","text":"a refusal?"}]},{"id":"blk-95298","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95300","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159364","text":"Is a second valued wire wanted, and if so which port pair — spinner→spinner (state to state) or"}]}],"id":"blk-95299","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-95301","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-159365","text":"spinner→relay (state onto a bit)?"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraxbs27coxchtahbwxlzjv3qflqjee5znzrih6qkybymotqihmx4qq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}